---
import Command from "./Command.astro";
import Window from "./Window.astro";
import Terminal from "./Terminal.astro";
import summary from "../samples/summary.ansi?raw";
---

<section class="hero">
  <div class="hero-copy">
    <p class="eyebrow">A context profiler for coding agents</p>
    <h1>Every session starts <em>pre-loaded.</em></h1>
    <p class="lede">
      Before you type, the harness fills the context window with layers: system prompt, built-in
      tools, MCP servers, instruction files, skills. Quench reads the session history Claude Code,
      Codex and Pi already keep, and shows what each layer takes.
    </p>
    <div class="hero-actions">
      <a class="btn" href="#install">Install</a>
      <Command text="quench" />
    </div>
    <ul class="facts">
      <li class="mcp">Read-only</li>
      <li class="tools">Zero setup</li>
      <li class="system">Stays on your machine</li>
    </ul>
  </div>
  <figure class="diagram">
    <Window />
    <figcaption>
      Fig. 1 — One demo session's first request, measured by <code>quench runs --json</code>. Layers
      sized by characters.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
  <div class="hero-term">
    <p class="callout">Run it with no arguments</p>
    <Terminal title="~/code/acme-api" command="quench" output={summary} class="term-hero" />
  </div>
</section>
